description:
Live Cacophony caravan #2210 has six members. `cara sync` refuses before mutation with:

`physical_sync_budget_insufficient: physical sync cannot enter its mutation phase without the reserved apply budget`

Receipt: 3,840,000ms required, 3,455,426ms remaining, 32 command slots. Repository config uses `sync.max_duration_secs: 3600` and `command_timeout_secs: 120`, so the fixed worst-case reservation 32*120s exceeds the entire operation budget before any mutation. Reservation scales with caravan size, making longer chains strictly less executable.

This blocked two already-planned cheap provider repairs after root #2208 merged: retarget new root #2210 from merged predecessor to main and arm squash auto-merge. An owner applied those manually; automatic chain handoff remains unproven.

Required fix:
- reserve against realistic planned operations and remaining budget, not every worst-case slot;
- allow a bounded mutation prefix for already-planned exact cheap repairs when total worst-case capacity exceeds the global budget;
- report any residual shortfall as typed per-caravan/per-operation diagnostics rather than refusing the whole sync run;
- preserve request/mutation caps, idempotency, exact head/base checks and no partial ambiguous mutation;
- tests for 6+ member caravans, near-deadline runs, two-provider-call root handoff, and true insufficient-budget refusal.

Coordinate release with bd-7546ea and bd-0629ce; do not mutate Cacophony provider state in tests.

Direct Harry resolution 2026-07-26, choice-019f9d34: strict FIFO is too broad. Recent Cara join semantics should prefer explicit `join` intent over older unjoined FIFO candidates. Current Cacophony proof: no caravans/problems, PR2113 is old inadmissible first row, and fully-green current-main PRs 2179/2191/2192 are rejected solely as non-canonical behind it; local cleanup must not force-merge/reorder as a substitute.

Required Cara product contract:
- distinguish explicit `join` intent from first-admission `new` intent before FIFO canonical-candidate rejection;
- when a valid target caravan exists and compatibility/dependency/policy checks pass, explicit join may attach ahead of unrelated unjoined FIFO candidates;
- FIFO still governs first admission/new-caravan intent; never skip a joined dependency, conflict, failed policy, provider/auth error, or ambiguous target;
- emit typed decision/provenance showing intent, target caravan, FIFO rows bypassed only because they are unjoined, compatibility, provider mutation, and idempotency;
- deterministic tests: older unjoined row + valid newer join; multiple caravans/ambiguous join; no caravan/new intent; conflicting join; joined ancestor/dependency; duplicate retry; stale pinned candidate; provider failure;
- audit Cacophony/Caravan Cara-version/store/config pins. Update exact reviewed pins for a 0.0.9 release; use first-party recovery and exact force-reintegration only for pinned generations proven incompatible, never blanket force/reorder;
- cut/review Cara 0.0.9 once, verify binary/assets/checksum/self-update and provider_mutated=false offline acceptance, deploy canonical Cacophony queue, then prove one ordinary join intent succeeds while unrelated unjoined FIFO rows remain ordered.

Coordinate with Cacophony bd-f4164e / bd-ab6fa6. Redundant PR closures are separate evidence-backed cleanup and do not satisfy this bead.

Operator hit `historical_current_pr_missing_caravan_label` running `cara join` on branch `pidaemon-aurora-workers`. GitHub has exactly one historical PR for that branch: PR #2016, merged 2026-07-18, unlabelled, remote head `a8c84c9`. The local prompt indicated a new commit ahead, but the remote branch still pointed at the merged generation.

`cara join --create-pr` already promises to create a PR when the current branch has no open PR, but historical branch resolution currently fails before the create path. Preserve the safety rule that Cara never labels/reopens a merged historical PR, while supporting a fresh generation on the same branch.

## Required behavior

When `join`/`rejoin --create-pr` is explicitly requested and no open PR maps the current branch/head:

- accept one exact same-repository merged historical PR as bounded ancestry evidence rather than current membership;
- require a named non-default branch, clean/safe worktree, and a local/provider head with commits beyond the merged historical head; exact old head/no diff fails closed;
- require the branch to be published non-interactively under an exact lease, or return a typed push-required continuation—never prompt or force-push;
- create one new open PR with the intended tail/default base, re-read exact provider facts, then continue the ordinary canonical-order/check/new-or-join preflight;
- only after all preconditions pass, retarget/rebase as configured, add `caravan`, disable non-head auto-merge, and write the durable membership audit comment;
- provider/head/base races and multiple historical candidates fail closed with completed-step receipts and idempotent retry guidance;
- plain `cara join` without `--create-pr` retains the current historical-navigation refusal.

Add CLI/JSON/MCP tests for merged branch + new commit, unchanged merged head, unpushed local head, branch reuse with one/multiple historical PRs, provider race, interrupted PR creation, and exact rerun idempotency.

Immediate workaround: publish the new commit (prefer a fresh branch name), create the new PR explicitly with `gh pr create`, then run `cara check --pr N` and `cara join`; Cara will add the membership label to the new open PR, never to merged PR #2016.
